  "notes": "・{呆|あき}れる → {呆|あき}れない (negative)\n・{呆|あき}れる → {呆|あき}れて (te-form)\n・{呆|あき}れる → {呆|あき}れた (past)\n・{呆|あき}れる → {呆|あき}れれば (conditional)\n\nKANJI:\nAlternative kanji: {惘|あき}れる (less common)\n\nUSAGE:\nUsually expresses negative surprise - disappointment, disgust, or exasperation at someone's behavior or a situation that defies common sense.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・〜に{呆|あき}れる (to be appalled at ~)\n・{呆|あき}れて{物|もの}が{言|い}えない (to be speechless with amazement)\n・{呆|あき}れるほど (appallingly, to an astonishing degree)\n・{呆|あき}れ{顔|がお} (look of disbelief)\n・{呆|あき}れ{果|は}てる (to be utterly appalled - intensified form)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n・{驚|おどろ}く - to be surprised (neutral)\n・{唖然|あぜん}とする - to be stunned, dumbfounded\n・{愕然|がくぜん}とする - to be shocked",
